    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0514" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg472"/>

                <head>Lord Lyons to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-12-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 9, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Her Majesty’s government having had under
                    their consideration the letter to the Secretary of the Navy, dated 31st of
                    October last, of which you were so good as to send a copy to Mr. Stuart on the
                    3d of last month, have seen with great satisfaction that you have requested the
                    Secretary of the Navy to issue instructions to the United States naval officers
                    not to search or open the public mails of any neutral or friendly power found on
                    board of captured vessels, but to send such mails to their destination as
                    quickly as maybe.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your most obedient, humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. H. Seward</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
